# AI ASSISTANT GUIDELINES (Vue 3 + Tailwind v4 POS System)

## 1. NEVER HALLUCINATE UI KIT VARIANTS
- You MUST ONLY use the allowed variants in `@/components/ui/AppButton.vue` (primary, secondary, danger, ghost, outline, success).
- DO NOT invent variants like `info` or `warning` for buttons unless you add them to the TypeScript definition first.

## 2. PRESERVE MODALS DURING LAYOUT REFACTORS
- When refactoring large pages (like `ProductsView.vue` or `PosView.vue`), BE EXTREMELY CAREFUL not to delete `<template>` modals located at the bottom of the file.
- ALWAYS extract everything from `<!-- Modal -->` to `</template>` before replacing the main grid/table layout.
- Vue 3 SFCs strictly require balanced HTML `</div>` tags. A single missed closing div will crash Vite.

## 3. STRICT COMPONENT REPLACEMENT
- DO NOT use generic regex (e.g. `re.sub`) for template replacement without strict start/end bounds. Use Python's `find()` to slice strings precisely.
